      "score": 34,
      "comments": 19,
      "author": "fanf",
      "published": "2026-10-08T19:06:25Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Root programs will cap public TLS certificate validity at 64 days by February 2027, down from the current 398 days.",
        "Automated renewal via ACME protocols or cert-manager becomes strictly mandatory, as manual certificate rotation cycles will cause production outages.",
        "Shorter lifespans limit exposure windows for compromised keys and mitigate reliance on unreliable CRL and OCSP revocation checks."
      ]
    },
